<title>USA: Buffets says merger hurt Q4.</title>
<headline>Buffets says merger hurt Q4.</headline>
<dateline>EDEN PRAIRIE, Minn. 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Buffets Inc, reporting lower 1996 fourth quarter earnings, cited inefficiencies and resulting higher costs following its merger with HomeTown Buffet Inc.</p>
<p>Buffets said Wednesday it was addressing the operating inefficiencies caused by the merger that raised costs.</p>
<p>Buffets operates 355 restaurants in 24 states and franchises 24 restaurants in 10 states.</p>
<p>Its shares were down 1/2 at 7-1/4 in afternoon trading.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
